---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
import { SITE, DONATE } from "../data/site";

/**
 * Terms of use and donor policy.
 *
 * NOTE FOR AVID: plain-language and honest, but not legal advice. Have this
 * reviewed by a Canadian lawyer, particularly the refund and receipting
 * sections, before you begin accepting donations at volume.
 */
const LAST_REVIEWED = "July 2026";
---

<Base
  title="Terms & Donor Policy"
  description="Terms of use for this website, and The AVID Foundation's donor policy: what a gift funds, what a donor receives, refunds, and receipting."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Terms"
    title="Terms of use and donor policy"
    lead={`How this site may be used, and what a gift to AVID does and does not entitle you to. Last reviewed ${LAST_REVIEWED}.`}
  />

  <section class="section grain">
    <div class="shell-narrow prose">
      <h2>Donor policy</h2>

      <h3>What your gift funds</h3>
      <p>
        Gifts are applied to programme delivery: refurbishing library spaces,
        furniture, book stock, cataloguing systems and staff training in the
        schools we work with, together with the monitoring and follow-up that
        keeps those libraries open.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where you fund a specific item — a shelf, a collection, a whole library —
        we assign it to a named school and report to you on that school. If a
        named project cannot proceed (for example, a school withdraws), we will
        contact you and either reassign your gift to a comparable project with
        your agreement, or refund it.
      </p>

      <h3>Tax receipts</h3>
      {
        DONATE.taxReceiptsAvailable ? (
          <p>
            {SITE.name} is a registered Canadian charity
            {SITE.charitableRegistrationNumber && (
              <> (registration no. {SITE.charitableRegistrationNumber})</>
            )}{" "}
            and issues official donation receipts for income tax purposes in
            accordance with Canada Revenue Agency requirements.
          </p>
        ) : (
          <>
            <p>
              <strong>
                We cannot currently issue official donation receipts for income
                tax purposes.
              </strong>{" "}
              AVID's application for registered-charity status with the Canada
              Revenue Agency is in progress. Under Canadian law, only a
              registered charity may issue official donation receipts, and we will
              not state or imply otherwise.
            </p>
            <p>
              For a gift made today you receive a written acknowledgement of the
              gift and a report naming the school it funded. Once registration is
              granted we will say so clearly on this site, and receipting will
              begin for gifts made from that date forward. A gift made before
              registration cannot be receipted retroactively.
            </p>
          </>
        )
      }

      <h3>Refunds</h3>
      <p>
        If you make a gift in error, or change your mind, email{" "}
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email.donate}`}>{SITE.email.donate}</a> within 30
        days and we will refund it in full, provided the funds have not already
        been disbursed to a project. Recurring gifts can be cancelled at any time
        and take effect before the next payment.
      </p>

      <h3>Anonymity and recognition</h3>
      <p>
        We name sponsors on a library's record only where the donor has asked us
        to. The default is that we do not publish your name. If you would like
        recognition, or would like it removed later, tell us and we will change
        it.
      </p>

      <h3>What a gift does not confer</h3>
      <p>
        A donation does not give a donor authority over which schools we select,
        which books we place, or how a project is run. Our board retains
        decision-making authority over all our resources — a requirement of
        Canadian charity law and, we think, the right way round. We welcome
        conversation and we do not accept direction.
      </p>
      <p>
        We decline gifts where accepting them would compromise our independence,
        our safeguarding obligations, or the interests of the schools we serve.
      </p>

      <h2>Terms of use</h2>

      <h3>About this site</h3>
      <p>
        This website is published by {SITE.name}, {SITE.location.line}. We aim to
        keep it accurate and current. Statistics cited are drawn from UNESCO,
        UNICEF and published Nigerian education statistics, with the source
        named where quoted.
      </p>

      <h3>Applications</h3>
      <p>
        Submitting a school application does not create any agreement between us
        and does not guarantee selection. We assess every application on need and
        eligibility, and we reply to all of them.
      </p>

      <h3>Content and copyright</h3>
      <p>
        Text and images on this site are the property of {SITE.name} or are used
        with permission. You are welcome to quote us, link to us, and reproduce
        short extracts with attribution — journalists, students and researchers
        especially. Please ask before reproducing photographs, because our
        permission to publish an image does not always extend to onward use.
      </p>
      <p>
        Book titles and authors named on this site are referenced for
        identification only; those works remain the property of their rights
        holders.
      </p>

      <h3>Links out</h3>
      <p>
        We link to other organisations where it is useful. We are not responsible
        for their content or their privacy practices.
      </p>

      <h3>Limits</h3>
      <p>
        We provide this site in good faith and without warranty. We are not liable
        for loss arising from reliance on information here, except where liability
        cannot be excluded by law.
      </p>

      <h3>Accessibility</h3>
      <p>
        This site is built to meet WCAG 2.1 Level AA. If any part of it is
        difficult for you to use, tell us at{" "}
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email.general}`}>{SITE.email.general}</a> — we
        treat that as a defect to be fixed, and we would rather hear about it than
        not.
      </p>

      <h3>Governing law</h3>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of the Province of Ontario and the
        federal laws of Canada.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
